WEBVTT

00:03.020 --> 00:05.980
You have absolutely no intention to repent,

00:05.980 --> 00:10.160
and you've made no effort
to improve your attitude.

00:10.160 --> 00:12.980
That's something I really like about you.

00:13.900 --> 00:16.370
But let me tell you one thing.

00:16.370 --> 00:21.250
You'll cause me a lot of trouble
if you pull something like that again.

00:21.530 --> 00:24.320
Because that isn't a part of my script.

00:25.840 --> 00:27.250
All right, you can go.

00:28.110 --> 00:28.900
Hmph.

00:33.130 --> 00:34.260
Well, then.

00:36.800 --> 00:38.980
What's on the books for today?

02:10.730 --> 02:11.440
<b>Maid Cafe & Bar
WELCOME HOME
 Would you like to play with
some maids?
 All-You-Can-Drink
1 Hour, 2000 Yen
Fuwa Fuwa!!
 Hours: 17:00-26:00</b>

02:23.240 --> 02:25.740
<b>New Release</b>

02:23.240 --> 02:25.740
<b>All the Rage!</b>

02:23.240 --> 02:25.740
<b>Cringemobile</b>

02:23.240 --> 02:25.740
<b>Open the Door to a New Age
Light Up the World</b>

02:36.160 --> 02:36.980
Anarchy-chan?

02:41.300 --> 02:43.540
What do you think, Otaku Hero,

02:44.200 --> 02:46.400
about that "Slayer" or whatever?

02:46.400 --> 02:49.560
Nobody ever told me we'd
have enemies like that.

02:49.560 --> 02:52.440
Yeah. I was surprised, too.

02:53.320 --> 02:57.820
Oh, did you come to check on me
because you were worried?

02:57.820 --> 02:59.090
Huh? Uh, yeah!

02:59.090 --> 03:03.060
The battles are probably gonna get
even worse from here on out, but...

03:03.580 --> 03:04.820
But...

03:04.820 --> 03:07.080
Let's all work together and do our best!

03:07.930 --> 03:11.600
Oh, come on! That's such a corny line.

03:12.200 --> 03:15.920
But... I guess I feel a little better now.

03:16.500 --> 03:17.720
Thanks.

03:20.790 --> 03:23.970
<i>I was going to ask her
to magically fix my broken toy,</i>

03:24.590 --> 03:26.980
<i>but it didn't feel like the right time.</i>

03:28.470 --> 03:29.660
Gobo.

03:30.200 --> 03:31.480
Can you fix it?

03:31.480 --> 03:38.620
Gobo gobo gobo gobo...

03:32.110 --> 03:38.620
"Resin parts deteriorate due to
UV exposure and plasticizer leakage."

03:38.620 --> 03:39.640
Hmm.

03:39.980 --> 03:44.050
Gobo gobo, gobogobo...

03:39.980 --> 03:44.050
"It's unavoidable when you're dealing
with toys and plastic models."

03:44.050 --> 03:45.250
Is it really?

03:45.250 --> 03:51.380
Gobogobo gobogobo...

03:45.960 --> 03:48.450
"When they shrink
and start to lose flexibility,

03:48.450 --> 03:51.380
they get very stiff
and become easier to break."

03:51.380 --> 03:51.970
What?!

03:51.970 --> 03:52.500
Huh?

03:52.500 --> 03:55.650
For me, stiff is so much better than limp and soft!

03:55.650 --> 03:57.380
Stop that talk right now!

03:57.380 --> 03:59.110
Do you think it can be fixed?

03:59.110 --> 04:03.440
Gobo gobo gobo gobo, gobo go go gobobo...

03:59.410 --> 04:03.440
"Chemical magic is actually my specialty."

04:03.440 --> 04:05.150
Oh, then please fix it!

04:06.140 --> 04:06.540
<b>Transform</b>

04:10.600 --> 04:10.770
<b>Self-Righteousness</b>

04:10.980 --> 04:11.180
<b>Hope</b>

04:11.600 --> 04:11.810
<b>Love</b>

04:12.140 --> 04:12.390
<b>Transience</b>

04:14.730 --> 04:15.150
<b>Transformation Complete</b>

04:23.080 --> 04:24.810
Wow, that's awesome!

04:28.840 --> 04:30.870
Whoa! What the what?!

04:36.610 --> 04:39.360
Toys these days sure are fancy.

04:39.360 --> 04:41.640
Pink-chan, what did you inject it with?

04:41.640 --> 04:44.420
Gobo gobo...

04:41.640 --> 04:44.420
"Self-rejuvenating magic for resin parts."

04:44.420 --> 04:46.510
There's <i>no</i> way that's all that was!

04:46.510 --> 04:53.520
Gobogobo, gobo gobo gobobobo...

04:47.360 --> 04:53.520
"Also Panax ginseng, pit viper elixir,
royal jelly, and a touch of energy magic."

04:53.520 --> 04:54.400
"Also—"

04:53.520 --> 04:55.520
Fine! I've heard enough.

04:57.600 --> 04:59.280
Wait for me!

05:07.030 --> 05:11.040
Oh, is this the scene where you you
get offered a silver and gold Godeen?

05:11.040 --> 05:13.110
I took such good care of it!

05:13.110 --> 05:16.930
I had to save up money
from my job just to buy a used one!

05:16.930 --> 05:18.560
Hold it!

05:20.780 --> 05:24.730
This right here's our turf.
Trespassers are not allowed!

05:24.730 --> 05:26.140
Who the hell are you?!

05:26.400 --> 05:29.140
We dwell here in the Akiba Liberated Zone.

05:29.380 --> 05:32.010
The Mansei Bridge Otaku Commune!

05:30.300 --> 05:32.010
Mansei Bridge Otaku Commune

05:32.020 --> 05:34.960
How lame. What do these old fogies want?

05:34.960 --> 05:36.140
Just like us,

05:36.140 --> 05:39.890
they must have run from Shobon's guys
and hid out here in the Liberated Zone.

05:39.890 --> 05:41.790
Why aren't we on the same side, then?!

05:41.790 --> 05:42.410
Hmph!

05:42.700 --> 05:45.670
It looks like we don't make
the grade for some reason.

05:45.670 --> 05:47.540
You mean like that "in-group hate" stuff?

05:47.540 --> 05:49.760
We're all otaku here, gang.

05:49.760 --> 05:51.160
That's right. Listen to me!

05:51.500 --> 05:53.920
I didn't come here to fight you.

05:53.920 --> 05:57.230
I only want to get my Godeen
that fell in the river.

05:57.500 --> 05:58.380
Unacceptable.

05:58.380 --> 05:58.920
Howat?

05:58.920 --> 05:59.630
Why?

05:59.960 --> 06:02.130
In the chaos of the riots three years ago,

06:02.660 --> 06:06.500
my brothers from another mother and I were
afraid our valuables would be confiscated,

06:06.500 --> 06:08.880
so we threw them all into the Kanda River.

06:09.510 --> 06:13.500
So the Kanda River is the final resting
place for countless historical artifacts.

06:13.500 --> 06:15.140
It's the ruins of Akihabara!

06:15.140 --> 06:15.840
That's right!

06:15.840 --> 06:17.500
You're just making excuses
to take our stuff!

06:17.500 --> 06:19.650
You're trying to sell them
on the net, even though

06:19.650 --> 06:22.220
you don't even know their value, I say!

06:22.220 --> 06:23.240
How did they know?

06:23.240 --> 06:24.120
No, we aren't, we aren't!

06:24.120 --> 06:26.070
So what he's saying is,

06:26.400 --> 06:29.360
we've got to beat them up and take it by force?

06:29.360 --> 06:32.900
We thought we heard some kind of crowd,
and once we got here...

06:32.900 --> 06:34.910
Goho, goho...

06:32.900 --> 06:34.910
"It reeked of old people."

06:35.180 --> 06:37.140
I kind of like that older-man smell, though.

06:37.140 --> 06:38.420
Nobody asked you!

06:38.420 --> 06:40.500
I don't care about your
stupid valuables or whatever.

06:40.500 --> 06:42.450
Rivers belong to everybody, right?

06:42.450 --> 06:45.800
What kind of adults would try
to monopolize a river?

06:45.800 --> 06:47.420
Damn you, magical girl!

06:47.420 --> 06:49.120
The scourge of all Akihabara!

06:49.120 --> 06:50.060
Huff! Puff!

06:50.360 --> 06:54.300
Anything else on your minds,
you middle-aged grunts?

06:54.300 --> 06:56.690
Yeah! Come get a piece of this, you brats!

06:56.680 --> 06:59.180
Menacing

06:59.190 --> 07:00.440
Hey! Stop it, stop it!

07:01.130 --> 07:03.700
These aren't the people
we need to be fighting.

07:03.700 --> 07:04.920
Are they?

07:06.450 --> 07:08.820
Then you gonna give up on Godeen?

07:08.820 --> 07:09.700
I don't know.

07:09.700 --> 07:11.460
Papa, please stop it!

07:11.460 --> 07:13.460
Th-That voice...

07:14.180 --> 07:14.960
It's you!

07:16.720 --> 07:20.200
Papa, please stop all this
and just come home!

07:21.430 --> 07:22.460
Drat!

07:22.460 --> 07:24.640
Mom is worried about you.

07:24.640 --> 07:26.590
Didn't I tell you
never to come here,

07:26.590 --> 07:27.100
Yumi?

07:27.100 --> 07:28.420
My name is Mai!

07:28.420 --> 07:31.620
Quit calling me the name of an
anime character from before I was born!

07:31.620 --> 07:34.610
Dad, I've been really worried about you, too!

07:34.610 --> 07:37.090
There is no longer any reason
for me to return, I say.

07:37.090 --> 07:39.870
Would you quit the "I say" stuff?
It's so embarrassing!

07:39.870 --> 07:41.860
You both need to go home, Mami-chan.

07:41.860 --> 07:45.140
Why do you keep calling me that? I'm Yu!

07:45.140 --> 07:47.110
Papa! Would you cut it out?!

07:47.110 --> 07:48.040
Come on!

07:48.040 --> 07:49.860
How can you act like this at your age?

07:48.730 --> 07:53.280
Oh, man. What have we walked into?

07:53.280 --> 07:56.320
It looks like some of them left
their families to come here.

07:56.320 --> 07:59.240
I don't care if they're married
or have kids. It doesn't matter!

07:59.240 --> 08:02.730
Even when we're persecuted,
we're determined to live as otaku!

08:02.730 --> 08:04.500
That makes us equals, right?

08:04.500 --> 08:07.160
I guess so. We're the same.

08:07.620 --> 08:09.270
We're all otaku.

08:09.560 --> 08:15.260
But then why are we having so much
trouble relating to those guys?

08:16.620 --> 08:19.020
The solution is simple, isn't it?

08:19.020 --> 08:20.040
Blue?

08:20.040 --> 08:21.760
It's been like this forever.

08:21.760 --> 08:24.780
The best way to become friends is...

08:26.020 --> 08:27.770
<b>Ba-thump! Kanda River Swim Meet
Full!? of Magical Girls</b>

08:30.780 --> 08:32.240
Good afternoon, ladies and gentlemen!

08:32.240 --> 08:34.110
It's about time to begin the Ba-thump!

08:34.110 --> 08:37.230
Kanda River Swim Meet Full of Magical Girls!

08:37.230 --> 08:38.920
You might even get to see something slip!

08:39.520 --> 08:41.570
All right!

08:42.710 --> 08:45.430
I'll knock you out!

08:45.970 --> 08:47.930
Gobo. Gobo.

08:47.930 --> 08:49.120
Yeah.

08:47.930 --> 08:49.120
Woo.

08:49.120 --> 08:52.690
The Revolutionary Otaku Army team
is all fired up and ready to go!

08:52.690 --> 08:54.420
How about the Otaku Commune side?

08:54.640 --> 08:57.080
A swim meet is a relatively crunk idea.

08:57.080 --> 08:59.480
Brings me right back to the '80s, I say!

08:59.480 --> 09:00.710
Wait, Papa!

09:02.690 --> 09:04.580
Why do we have to play?

09:04.580 --> 09:06.930
Why am I even dressed like this?

09:06.930 --> 09:08.590
You're doin' great, Mami-chan!

09:08.590 --> 09:10.150
They're all fired up, too!

09:10.960 --> 09:12.660
But why a swim meet?

09:12.660 --> 09:15.670
Old timers used to say
that skin-to-skin contact

09:15.670 --> 09:18.900
is the best way to get to know someone.

09:18.900 --> 09:24.160
In the past, the Kanda River was full of
industrial waste and household wastewater.

09:24.160 --> 09:27.670
It was called the river of death,
as no living creature could survive in it.

09:27.670 --> 09:29.600
But in 1987,

09:29.600 --> 09:32.920
the Ochiai Water Reclamation Center
started advanced wastewater treatment,

09:32.920 --> 09:35.780
and the water became so clean
it was almost unrecognizable.

09:35.780 --> 09:39.180
So clean, in fact, that it
is now possible to hold swim meets.

09:39.180 --> 09:40.490
What he said.

09:40.490 --> 09:41.430
Seriously?

09:41.430 --> 09:42.930
Onto the first game!

09:42.850 --> 09:45.310
<b>Wobbly Floating
Obstacle Race!!</b>

09:42.930 --> 09:45.310
The Wobbly Floating Obstacle Race!

09:45.310 --> 09:46.890
Yay!

09:46.890 --> 09:50.880
Contestants must race toward the
goal across platforms placed in the water,

09:50.880 --> 09:52.640
all while avoiding various obstacles!

09:52.640 --> 09:55.030
Well then, on your marks,

09:52.650 --> 09:56.780
<b>START</b>

09:55.350 --> 09:56.780
get set...

09:56.780 --> 09:58.240
Go for it, Blue!

09:58.240 --> 09:59.060
No problem!

09:59.430 --> 10:01.300
Go forth, I say, my son!

10:01.300 --> 10:02.540
Good luck, Mami-chan!

10:02.540 --> 10:03.450
What did I say?!

10:03.450 --> 10:04.620
Start!

10:05.080 --> 10:06.320
Oh, stop!

10:06.320 --> 10:07.440
Wah!

10:08.580 --> 10:11.330
Oh, staahp!

10:11.330 --> 10:13.330
Whoa!

10:13.330 --> 10:15.220
Unghh! They're staring at me!

10:15.220 --> 10:17.460
They're watching me get totally humiliated!

10:17.460 --> 10:20.960
Oh, please! Please stop
branding me with your hot gaze!

10:20.960 --> 10:23.470
Wait, stare more!

10:32.160 --> 10:33.980
Why is this happening to me?

10:41.130 --> 10:43.440
I... have lost!

10:43.830 --> 10:44.910
<b>Contestant Blue Retires!!</b>

10:44.800 --> 10:46.370
The Commune for the win!

10:44.910 --> 10:46.370
<b>Contestant Blue Retires!!</b>

10:46.370 --> 10:48.120
All right!

10:46.370 --> 10:48.120
We did won!

10:48.120 --> 10:49.920
God damn it!

10:49.920 --> 10:51.120
I don't get this game.

10:51.120 --> 10:52.620
Onto the next game!

10:52.620 --> 10:55.120
Jiggle-Joggle Water Sumo!

10:52.710 --> 10:55.130
<b>Jiggle!?Joggle!?
Water Sumo!</b>

10:55.130 --> 11:00.130
<b>Mainofuji</b>

10:55.480 --> 11:00.500
From the west, Mainofuji.

11:00.500 --> 11:05.480
From the east, Asapinkryu.

11:03.930 --> 11:06.640
<b>Asapinkryu</b>

11:05.480 --> 11:06.640
Gobo!

11:06.640 --> 11:08.040
Go, Pink!

11:08.040 --> 11:09.230
Something doesn't look right.

11:09.230 --> 11:12.460
All right, hands down, energy up...

11:12.460 --> 11:15.900
Still in! Still in, still in, still in!

11:15.900 --> 11:17.950
Still in! Still in!

11:17.950 --> 11:19.690
There's no way!

11:20.870 --> 11:22.280
Gobo!

11:22.280 --> 11:25.010
Asapinkryu!

11:22.950 --> 11:26.410
<b>Victor
Asapinkryu</b>

11:25.010 --> 11:26.400
Um,

11:26.400 --> 11:28.920
I found this on the ground.

11:29.670 --> 11:30.650
Could it be?

11:30.650 --> 11:31.920
That's the medicine Pink-chan

11:31.920 --> 11:34.160
shoots up when she wants to feel good!

11:34.160 --> 11:38.350
Eh, the round did go to Asapinkryu,

11:38.350 --> 11:40.950
but due to violation
of no-doping regulations,

11:40.950 --> 11:42.720
Mainofuji wins!

11:42.720 --> 11:45.470
Wow! Yay!

11:43.100 --> 11:44.430
You did it, Emi!

11:44.430 --> 11:45.480
What did I say?!

11:45.480 --> 11:46.920
Pink!

11:46.920 --> 11:49.140
No doping! Ever!

11:49.140 --> 11:50.720
And now, the final game!

11:50.720 --> 11:53.240
Pruned! Wet Chicken Fight!

11:50.730 --> 11:53.230
<b>Pruned! Wet Chicken Fight</b>

11:53.240 --> 11:56.730
First to three points wins,
so we may see an upset!

11:56.730 --> 11:59.480
Both teams, on your marks,

11:59.480 --> 12:01.040
start!

12:01.930 --> 12:05.160
Right after these commercials.

12:04.490 --> 12:05.990
<b>Up Next:
Something Terrible Happens!?</b>

12:08.400 --> 12:12.760
Well then, once again,
we're back to the wet chicken fight.

12:13.070 --> 12:17.250
A team wins when they take their
opponent's hat or knock the other team over.

12:17.490 --> 12:21.010
On your marks, get set...

12:21.010 --> 12:22.760
Stuartro!

12:24.270 --> 12:26.400
Let's go, Blue-chan! Pink-chan!

12:26.400 --> 12:27.360
Yo!

12:26.400 --> 12:27.360
Gobobo!

12:27.360 --> 12:28.780
Counting on you, Anarchy-chan!

12:28.780 --> 12:31.030
Leave it to me!

12:35.240 --> 12:37.400
Damn it! That isn't fair, you two!

12:37.400 --> 12:40.040
Why do I have to do this?

12:40.570 --> 12:45.320
I totally believe that this
will help us get along better!

12:45.320 --> 12:46.640
Horse crap!

12:46.640 --> 12:49.080
You and I are fundamentally different!

12:49.080 --> 12:50.580
I don't think that at all!

12:50.580 --> 12:54.070
Exactly what is so
different between you and me?

12:54.070 --> 12:56.070
If you don't know, I shall tell you.

12:56.070 --> 12:58.120
Otaku hobbies are accepted these days.

12:58.120 --> 13:01.460
People speak of them like
they're any common hobby.

13:01.460 --> 13:05.260
In the past, otaku were gloomy
folks who avoided other people.

13:05.260 --> 13:08.480
They pursued their hobbies
quietly and in private!

13:08.470 --> 13:11.970
<b>Advance Interview!!</b>

13:08.480 --> 13:11.970
We collected information
in the shadows, hiding from the public,

13:11.970 --> 13:14.230
bought merchandise
with our faces covered up,

13:14.230 --> 13:16.520
and if we slipped up
and were exposed to others,

13:16.520 --> 13:19.100
we'd be labeled "grody!" and ostracized.

13:19.100 --> 13:21.640
We lived through
an extremely challenging age!

13:21.970 --> 13:22.870
However,

13:22.860 --> 13:25.860
<b>Kiss!</b>

13:22.870 --> 13:27.630
today's otaku can acquire quality
merchandise and reliable info freely,

13:25.860 --> 13:29.120
<b>Title Search</b>

13:25.860 --> 13:29.120
<b>Figurines</b>

13:25.860 --> 13:29.120
<b>Plastic Models</b>

13:25.860 --> 13:29.120
<b>Male Characters</b>

13:25.860 --> 13:29.120
<b>Female Characters</b>

13:25.860 --> 13:29.120
<b>Stores</b>

13:25.860 --> 13:29.120
<b>Figurines</b>

13:25.860 --> 13:29.120
<b>Plastic Models</b>

13:27.630 --> 13:29.120
without any true effort!

13:29.120 --> 13:31.080
They assemble on the street in daylight,

13:31.080 --> 13:35.610
and furthermore, even have the nerve
to take pride in being otaku!

13:35.610 --> 13:39.370
It's as if they're bragging,
"my hobby isn't gross!"

13:39.370 --> 13:42.270
But otaku are all still
being persecuted today.

13:42.270 --> 13:44.250
So there's no reason for us to fight!

13:45.240 --> 13:48.300
That persecution is because you young otaku

13:48.300 --> 13:50.760
couldn't figure it out
and tried to stick out!

13:51.480 --> 13:52.510
Open your eyes!

13:52.880 --> 13:55.650
Otaku are beings that should
not see the light of day!

13:55.650 --> 13:58.640
To hell with "otaku culture" and "Akiba culture"!

13:58.640 --> 14:01.590
Why haven't you realized
that the recognition you

14:01.590 --> 14:03.720
think you finally earned
is only an illusion!

14:06.400 --> 14:09.400
Hey, Otaku Hero! I'm losing it!

14:09.400 --> 14:14.400
You can't actually believe that
everything happening now is because of us?!

14:14.400 --> 14:15.920
In my own case,

14:15.920 --> 14:19.040
I didn't want to leave my family
and come to a place like this.

14:19.040 --> 14:19.970
'Tis true.

14:19.970 --> 14:23.420
Due to the recent incident,
otaku, like ourselves, who have families

14:23.420 --> 14:26.190
were forced to confess
their true otaku nature,

14:26.190 --> 14:29.250
after keeping it hidden for so long!

14:28.930 --> 14:32.680
<b>Spited Away</b>

14:29.250 --> 14:31.280
To confess that we like anime,
we like tokusatsu,

14:30.800 --> 14:34.180
<b>Animaje</b>

14:31.280 --> 14:34.280
we adore magical girls
with colorful hairstyles!

14:34.280 --> 14:37.270
To confess that our storage rooms
are full of old posters,

14:37.270 --> 14:40.430
store displays, and drama LPs!

14:40.430 --> 14:44.440
I still have nightmares on the regular
of my family's reactions when they found out.

14:44.440 --> 14:46.040
It was already totally obvious!

14:46.040 --> 14:50.440
At Obon and New Year's you'd always go,
"I'm off to Odaiba, I say!" and leave us!

14:50.440 --> 14:55.460
If not for these circumstances,
I never would have lost my family!

14:57.720 --> 14:59.700
But now and then are different!

15:00.200 --> 15:04.040
Why aren't you happier
that we can watch anime

15:04.040 --> 15:06.460
and buy merch without any resistance now?

15:06.460 --> 15:09.210
Otaku shouldn't have to sneak around
and hide from society.

15:09.600 --> 15:12.720
We should... hold our heads up high!

15:12.720 --> 15:14.680
Aah! His youth is overpowering!

15:14.680 --> 15:15.980
It's blinding, I say!

15:15.980 --> 15:17.400
That's good, that's good!

15:17.400 --> 15:18.510
That's the spirit!

15:18.510 --> 15:20.300
Most importantly,

15:20.300 --> 15:23.240
right now we have magical girls
who never existed before with us.

15:23.240 --> 15:25.480
If you really do like magical girls,

15:25.480 --> 15:28.360
then join these three
real-life magical girls

15:28.360 --> 15:31.040
and help us reclaim the world we want!

15:31.040 --> 15:32.860
Ridiculous!

15:32.860 --> 15:36.160
Magical girls belong in anime!
They belong in manga!

15:36.160 --> 15:38.280
They shine because they are a fantasy!

15:38.280 --> 15:40.760
Magical girls in real life?
Perish the thought!

15:40.760 --> 15:44.000
They haven't even the power to light
a grain-of-wheat bulb, I say!

15:44.000 --> 15:45.630
Or to rephrase...

15:45.630 --> 15:47.120
...they lack elegance!

15:47.120 --> 15:49.270
Gobo gobo.

15:47.720 --> 15:49.270
"What the hell are they on about?"

15:50.810 --> 15:52.390
<i>That</i> part got to you?

15:52.390 --> 15:54.510
Hold on, Otaku Hero! Wha—!

15:54.510 --> 15:56.840
Otaku Hero-sama, hold it together!

15:56.840 --> 16:00.020
Oops! The Revolutionary Army is in a pinch!

16:00.960 --> 16:05.780
I know that we've lived in different times
and might not see eye-to-eye,

16:05.780 --> 16:09.840
but all we want is a world
where we can like what we want to like!

16:09.840 --> 16:12.530
I know we're fighting for the same thing!

16:17.530 --> 16:20.970
<i>Maybe we'll never be able to get along.</i>

16:30.820 --> 16:32.290
SSC!

16:30.820 --> 16:32.290
Gobo gobo!

16:33.430 --> 16:36.050
Sorry to interrupt your playtime,

16:36.450 --> 16:39.290
but I have plans, too, you know.

16:39.920 --> 16:40.820
Oh, boy!

16:40.820 --> 16:43.350
Three giant mecha have suddenly appeared!

16:43.350 --> 16:46.570
Whatever will happen to the swim meet?

16:48.080 --> 16:49.850
T-Take cover!

16:52.440 --> 16:53.700
Why now?

16:53.700 --> 16:55.120
Pull your head outta your ass!

16:55.120 --> 16:57.990
Now isn't the time
to feel sorry for yourself!

16:57.990 --> 16:59.820
A-All right. Let's get them!

16:59.820 --> 17:00.710
Transform!

16:59.820 --> 17:00.710
Gobogobo!

17:02.700 --> 17:03.700
<b>Transform</b>

17:11.590 --> 17:11.960
<b>Self-Righteousness</b>

17:12.380 --> 17:12.760
<b>Hope</b>

17:13.630 --> 17:14.010
<b>Love</b>

17:14.720 --> 17:15.220
<b>Transience</b>

17:19.800 --> 17:20.720
<b>Transformation Complete</b>

17:23.020 --> 17:24.600
The swimsuit versions!

17:26.360 --> 17:27.650
Let's get 'em, girls!

17:27.650 --> 17:28.650
Gobo!

17:27.650 --> 17:28.650
Hell yeah!

17:38.230 --> 17:39.120
Girls!

17:41.630 --> 17:45.860
Unghh, they have the upper hand underwater!

17:47.450 --> 17:49.800
Papa, aren't you going to help them?

17:50.880 --> 17:54.640
It's their fault that
the world turned out this way.

17:54.640 --> 18:00.130
But the magical girls
are fighting as hard as they can!

18:02.130 --> 18:04.440
If we got rid of the water, they'd be toast!

18:04.440 --> 18:06.680
Gobobobobo gobobo. Bogo bogo!

18:06.680 --> 18:09.040
Seriously? That might work!

18:13.240 --> 18:16.240
Girls!

18:18.700 --> 18:19.490
Is this my...

18:19.490 --> 18:20.860
Godeen!

18:20.860 --> 18:23.340
I'm so glad I found you!

18:29.960 --> 18:31.120
And is that...

18:31.620 --> 18:32.750
Godeen?!

18:33.920 --> 18:38.200
That's the Popopi corporation's
original Deluxe Super-Die-Cast Godeen!

18:38.200 --> 18:39.130
What's that?

18:39.450 --> 18:42.470
The Banban Godeens that
circulate today are only remakes

18:42.780 --> 18:50.220
of the mega-hit Super-Die-Cast Series
developed by the Popopi corporation long ago!

18:50.220 --> 18:51.880
The Kanda River is amazing!

18:51.880 --> 18:54.480
The resting place
of countless treasures, I say!

18:54.480 --> 18:58.640
Gobo bogo.

18:54.960 --> 18:58.640
"That old toy absorbed
a shot of my special medicine."

18:58.640 --> 19:01.240
So doping is allowed for some things?!

19:02.520 --> 19:05.420
The ancient one has protected the newcomer.

19:05.420 --> 19:06.620
Well...

19:06.960 --> 19:10.480
...a world where we can like
what we want to like!

19:10.480 --> 19:12.870
I know we're fighting for the same thing!

19:12.870 --> 19:13.890
Papa!

19:13.890 --> 19:15.010
Leader!

19:15.010 --> 19:15.880
Mister!

19:20.380 --> 19:21.630
Damn it!

19:21.630 --> 19:23.410
We need to make an opening!

19:23.410 --> 19:25.020
Here we come!

19:28.480 --> 19:29.520
Oh, no way!

19:31.020 --> 19:33.280
Metamorphose, I say!

19:34.580 --> 19:35.780
Do Whatcha!

19:36.950 --> 19:40.520
Twirly-Twirly Tokimeki Makeup!

19:42.780 --> 19:45.030
Don't tell me they're...

19:45.030 --> 19:46.580
...transforming?

19:48.540 --> 19:49.440
Ka-ching!

19:49.440 --> 19:50.680
Nah, of course not.

19:50.680 --> 19:52.080
Yeah, right?

19:52.510 --> 19:53.540
Papa!

19:52.510 --> 19:53.540
Dad!

20:00.260 --> 20:01.420
Good heavens.

20:01.910 --> 20:03.160
Okay, here we go!

20:04.170 --> 20:05.440
The death blow!

20:07.610 --> 20:09.940
Whoa! What just happened?!

20:18.680 --> 20:19.960
Combined magic!

20:18.680 --> 20:22.200
Gobogobo gobo! Gobo gobobo
gobo gobobo gobo gobobo!

20:18.940 --> 20:22.200
<b>Combined Magic!!
We Sucked All the
Water Out of the River!</b>

20:19.960 --> 20:22.200
We sucked all the water out of the river!

20:22.200 --> 20:23.130
You did it!

20:22.200 --> 20:23.200
<b>Combined Magic!!
We Sucked All the
Water Out of the River!</b>

20:23.130 --> 20:23.950
My word!

20:25.530 --> 20:28.080
You sure had your way with us.

20:28.080 --> 20:29.530
Now we turn you into sashimi.

20:29.530 --> 20:30.750
Gobo-bo!

20:36.790 --> 20:39.800
<b>Dancer Mask</b>

20:36.790 --> 20:39.800
<b>The Legendary Show Now In a Box Set</b>

20:36.790 --> 20:39.800
<b>Laserdisc</b>

20:36.790 --> 20:39.800
This is the Dancer Mask LD box!

20:39.800 --> 20:42.300
This is a real VHD player!

20:42.300 --> 20:45.300
It's a mountain of treasure!

20:45.300 --> 20:48.540
Dad, you were so cool... I say!

20:48.960 --> 20:50.840
I'm glad you're okay, Papa.

20:50.840 --> 20:53.160
Sorry to make you worry, Emi.

20:55.120 --> 20:56.340
Thank you.

20:56.800 --> 20:59.970
With your help, we were
able to defeat the enemy.

21:00.480 --> 21:01.690
Brave Godeen...

21:01.960 --> 21:05.450
When I watched the reruns as a kid,
I thought he was so cool.

21:06.200 --> 21:11.320
You know, back then it never mattered
if you were an otaku or not.

21:11.590 --> 21:15.580
We could all like what we wanted to
like as much as we wanted.

21:18.060 --> 21:21.330
I do want us to fight on the same side.

21:22.920 --> 21:24.840
Don't misunderstand this.

21:25.390 --> 21:27.350
The only reason we lent a hand this time

21:27.350 --> 21:30.750
was to protect the
Kanda River's historical artifacts.

21:30.750 --> 21:33.350
It wasn't to help the likes of you!

21:33.350 --> 21:34.880
Fall back!

21:38.150 --> 21:41.480
I still think that someday
we'll be able to get along!

21:41.970 --> 21:43.730
I truly believe we will!

23:25.830 --> 23:28.690
Beyond the city, yet another closed city.

23:28.690 --> 23:30.090
Walls frozen solid.

23:30.090 --> 23:33.110
Blow open a hole to let fresh air into a closed heart.

23:33.110 --> 23:35.350
Inside Mecca, a sleeping MacGuffin.

23:35.350 --> 23:37.580
Climbing to acquire an item.

23:37.580 --> 23:40.000
Yet another incident.
